{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ page_title }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1 class="display-4 mb-4" style="color: #155263;">{{ page_title }}</h1>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <p class="lead">
                Welcome to our simple **Symfony Gallery application**, built as an educational project.
                Our goal is to demonstrate key techniques used in modern Symfony applications,
                specifically: **modular Twig**, **Dependency Injection (DI)**, and **secure file handling**.
            </p>

            <h2 class="mt-5" style="color: #1e758d;">Our Architecture</h2>
            <p>
                The application relies on **Bootstrap 5** for full responsiveness and utilizes the **Controller-View** pattern (MVC-like).
                All uploaded files are securely stored outside of Git control, adhering to best practices.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-unstyled">
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> **Controllers:** Use of `#[Route]` attributes and service injection (e.g., `SluggerInterface`).</li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> **Views:** Architecture with inheritance (`base.html.twig`) and composition (`_navbar.html.twig`).</li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success" style="color: #ffbb09;"></i> **Forms:** Handling single data (gallery name) and file collections (pictures) with validation.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card shadow-sm border-0" style="background-color: #ffd76f;">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="color: #0c2f39;">Symfony Core</h5>
                    <p class="card-text small">Version: 6.x / 7.x</p>
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="color: #0c2f39;">Front-end</h5>
                    <p class="card-text small">Framework: Bootstrap 5</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}